 "notes": [
  "Retroactively renamed from the plain key \"ישם\" to \"ישם²\" when H3455 (\"place; be placed\") was added to the dataset as \"ישם¹\" -- true homograph, per the root-key superscript convention (lower Strong's number gets ¹). The two are spelled identically once niqqud is stripped (this root's own headword is יָשַׁם, shin; H3455's is יָשַׂם, sin), so the plain, undifferentiated key would otherwise collide."
